the three patches applied to the tree. Recopy from there rather than editing
here, and recopy the whole directory rather than a file, so the two can never
drift a file at a time.

The three `PATCH-*.diff` files in `src/city/vendored/` travel with the source
because they describe what was changed and why. They are not applied here:
the tree is already patched.

## RaceGOW5 Track 1

    Series      RaceGOW, an at home whoop time trial series
    Track       RaceGOW5 Track 1, designed by Skittles
    Source      racegow.com/tracks, the official Track 1 animation
    Held at     src/room-data.js, generated by scripts/bake-room.js

The fifth act flies a real published track rather than an invented one. What
is reproduced is a set of DIMENSIONS: where a gate stands, how high its sill
is, and which side of a pole the line goes. RaceGOW publishes its tracks
precisely so that everybody can build them, which is the whole premise of the
series, and the credit here is the one the series itself gives: the designer
by name, and the organiser's own figures for the pipe and the opening.

The numbers are not read from RaceGOW directly. They come from
`Mathew-Harvey/WebFPVSimulator`, which is the copy of record for this project
and carries its own citations in `src/trackbuilder/racegow.js` and
`src/trackbuilder/presets.js`, and the simulator credits andAgainFPV for
bringing the track over. Regenerate rather than edit, so the front door and
the simulator cannot come to disagree about where a gate is.

